{"type":"step-attempt","step":"cross-boundary-invariants","sessionId":"b9e882e5-9768-4b28-8f4c-8956994f0358","outcome":{"verdict":"escalation","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/auth-setup-ux/cross-boundary-invariants-result-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":false,"findings":[{"severity":"medium","resolution":"fixable","file":"src/util/secret-input.ts","title":"TTY raw mode not restored on SIGTERM during `credentials set` input","rationale":"`readTTY` calls `input.setRawMode(true)` and restores it only via in-band stdin data events (Ctrl-C, Enter, EOT, stream error). There is no `process.on('SIGTERM', ...)` or `process.on('exit', ...)` guard. The unchanged dispatch mechanism (`bin/specrunner.ts`) adds no signal handlers around command handlers. If `credentials set` is killed via SIGTERM while blocking on TTY input, `setRawMode(false)` is never called and the terminal is left in raw mode, making the session unusable. Implicit invariant broken: 'a process that enables TTY raw mode restores it before exit, regardless of how exit occurs.'","line":83},{"severity":"medium","resolution":"decision-needed","file":"src/cli/command-registry.ts","title":"`--provider github` deprecated flag gives incorrect migration guidance","rationale":"The single deprecated message ('specrunner login is GitHub-only now. To store a Claude Code token for headless runs, use: specrunner credentials set claude-code') is accurate for `--provider claude` but wrong for `--provider github`. Before this PR, `login --provider github` was equivalent to `login` (GitHub Device Flow). After this PR it throws FlagParseError with the claude-code guidance. The unchanged `bin/specrunner.ts` FlagParseError handler writes this message verbatim to stderr. A user who ran `login --provider github` is told to run `credentials set claude-code` (wrong); the correct action is just `specrunner login` with no flag. Design D2 deliberately chose a single message as a simplification trade-off.","line":489,"options":[{"label":"Keep current behavior — accept the imprecision","consequence":"Users who pass `--provider github` see misleading guidance. Impact is low because `--provider github` is rarely used (most docs show bare `specrunner login`) and LOGIN_USAGE that follows shows the correct syntax."},{"label":"Append clarification for the `--provider github` case","consequence":"Deprecated message becomes: '...use: specrunner credentials set claude-code. If you previously passed --provider github, just run: specrunner login.' Stays within D2 (single message), removes wrong guidance. Requires updating the test that pins the message content."}]}],"evidence":{"checked":18,"skipped":0,"unverified":0},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/doctor/next-steps.ts","title":"RULES step prescriptions not covered by hint-command-existence machine test","rationale":"TC-014 (`tests/hint-command-existence.test.ts`) scans `src/core/doctor/**` only for `hint:` string fields, not the `RULES` step strings in `next-steps.ts`. Both referenced commands (`specrunner login`, `specrunner init`) remain valid so there is no current bug. Pre-existing gap not introduced by this PR."},{"severity":"low","file":"src/util/secret-input.ts","title":"Non-TTY path calls `input.resume()` without subsequent `pause()`","rationale":"`readNonTTY` calls `(input as {resume?}).resume()` to ensure the stream emits data, but does not re-pause stdin after reading. This leaves `process.stdin` in a flowing state for the process lifetime. Harmless for a top-level CLI command (process exits immediately after), but noted as a potential concern if `runCredentialsSet` were ever embedded."}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-16T06:40:18.593Z","endedAt":"2026-08-16T06:51:02.655Z"}
